+\begin{resumo}[ABSTRACT]
+\begin{otherlanguage*}{english}
+This work presents Luminthor, a textual integrated development environment
+(IDE) for practicing programming logic on Android. The research problem is
+to combine editing, analysis, messages in Portuguese, and execution visualization
+in an application with local processing. The objective is to develop this
+integration through the educational Lumi language, a Rust engine, and a Flutter
+interface, connected by a foreign function interface (FFI). This is applied
+technological research with exploratory objectives; it combines bibliographic
+research, artifact development, and a questionnaire survey, using descriptive
+quantitative analysis supported by qualitative comments. The application
+combines an editor with code completion and code templates, local file
+management, messages in Portuguese, token and abstract syntax tree visualization,
+and a debugger with a navigable execution trace, alongside a learning path
+with six modules and 18 lessons. Verification on November 15, 2026, passed
+68 Rust tests and 159 Flutter tests, with no issues reported by Flutter static
+analysis. Data collection from November 9 to 13 received 12 submissions, with
+one refusal excluded; of the 11 consenting respondents, eight reported installing
+and opening the application and answered the eight usability items. Medians
+ranged from 4.5 to 5.0 on the five-point scale, with six to eight favorable
+responses per item. Comments indicated priorities concerning navigation,
+debugger identification, typing, and interpretation of one diagnostic. The
+small sample, predominance of prior experience, and incomplete reports restrict
+the evaluation to perceived usability, without establishing learning gains or
+performance on devices. The technological contribution is the integration of
+editing, local processing, execution inspection, and educational content in
+a mobile environment.
+
+\par\vspace{0.6cm}\noindent\textbf{Keywords}: programming education; educational interpreters; mobile devices; development environments; programming logic.
+\end{otherlanguage*}
+\end{resumo}
